## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides; tier 2, so short)
- **G-1 delta (C1).** A path beyond the two, a product, package or config byte = **Blocker**; any removed line or an old row changed = **Major, class (d)**; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card slug in an added line or a commit message = **Blocker**; a third commit or a moved head = STOP; a Jira key or work number in an added line or a commit message = **Minor** (the PR title's two ticket keys: **Minor**, Tuesday edits it); non-ASCII or a tab in the added lines = **Major**.
- **G-2 the rows against plants (C2).** *Classification rule:* a shape is **IN the family** when it makes the wait end before a delayed digest has settled, drops the delay's effect or breaks the verdict list (b116), or changes the in-string decision of the scanner line 122 or any of the twelve Done-when shapes (b616); **OUT** when it edits another scanner line, a shape beyond the twelve, a product file or a flag. The slow row not red under P1 = **Major, class (a)**; the slow row red under P3 or P3a (the row bites something other than the delay) = **Major, class (b)**; the slow row red unplanted or a new row red at main's product = **Major, class (c)**; the control row green at a constant of 0 or 3500 = **Major, class (a)**; an old b116 row red under P1, P1x, P3 or P3a (so the premise "old rows do not bite at zero delay" is false) = a **Note** with the cell (and the "new row" claim of the PR re-graded); the new b616 row not red under W028c, or red under an unrelated plant it is not named for = **Major**; a Done-when shape no longer red under its own swap at head = **Major, class (a)** (a builder claim contradicted); an IN-family K shape that changes the answer and leaves all 56 green = **Major, class (a)**; an old-file red set not a subset of the new = **Major**; a thrown-from-helper red (instead of the verdict assertion) = a **Note** (the kind is named); a predicted-equivalent (B648-5) red = **Major** with the measurement; a control that cannot fail (c2, c4, c5) = the run is DEAD (NOT TESTED) and for c4 a **Major** of its own. An OUT shape green on all rows = **Note**.
- **G-3 counts, load and CI (C3, C4).** The b116 file other than 8 of 8, the b616 file other than 56 of 56, without a reason = a finding at the severity of its cause; the unit counts other than main + 2 passed = **Major**; lint/format/typecheck non-zero at the head and zero at main = **Major**; a new row red in any run of the load loop (b116 file x12 at head) = **Major, class (b)** with the cell (a new timing flake in the file PCOMP-62 is about), a red at main's file in the same loop = a **Note**; **ANOMALY 2: the engine timing test red at MAIN under the same hog = a Note with ticket text (the cell, the file blob equal at main and head, the failing message, the cap), red ONLY at the head (every head run of the cell, no main run, n >= 3 engine-file or n >= 2 chain runs per side) = a Blocker, both red = a Note with the two cells, not reproduced = a Note ("not reproduced in n runs"); the chain WITHOUT the hog not green at head = a Major (a Blocker if it is green at main)**; a whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; a load-only red = artefact (record both runs); a failing check-run on the head = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS (conditional); an open alert on the PR ref = **Blocker** and a STOP; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with another open PR or live lane = **Major**; a missing PRIOR WORK = returned. **Always Note:** dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the unit chain's one explicit-run skip, the unfilled `@@` placeholders of the builder STATUS (ANOMALY 1; a Note under Corrections, since you read CodeQL yourself).
- **G-4 words (C5, C7).** A commit-message sentence a run does not carry = **Major (class e)**; a PR title or body sentence a run does not carry = **Minor** (Tuesday edits it), except the body's "from an engine timing test outside this change", which is graded by the ANOMALY 2 cell (a Blocker cell makes it Major); a title or comment that claims more than its rows assert = **Minor** when wording only and the row it names does assert its own claim, **Major, class (b)** only if a shape the title names is green; a builder claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number.
- **G-5 the verdict follows the table, and the cap.** Any Blocker or any Major of the class = `NO GO round 1 of 2`: FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list (with cells), the RESIDUE as ticket text with the tester's cells attached, and the fix shape in prose (one new commit on the same branch; a second NO GO on this class is a STOP to Tuesday under the cap). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS` (list the Deferred rows). Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` is always conditional.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route; the demo-deploy seat may be live and uses no local heavy job)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 7.32 at the draft: expect waits). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, any vitest over more than one file, the unit chain, the plant sets, the hog cells. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, the clone, C4 polls, C5/C6/C7 reads). **One heavy job of yours at a time, behind `.tools/b993/lock` AND the project lock above (FIFO with any other Composer seat).** A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b993/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; a wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line. Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). **The hog of C3b is the one artificial load: it lives inside ONE capped container, never on the host; it is started and stopped by the job, and nothing of it outlives the run.** Build `pc-b993-node:head` once from the head's tree: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b993-node:head <tree>` (ABSOLUTE `-f`; `npm ci` must be CACHED); if the daemon is down, say so and start Docker Desktop. **Budget (write it at Step 0, before the first heavy job): image 1 (2 at most); baselines 4 (b116 and b616 at main, unit at main, unit at head); head file counts 3 + 3 + rows alone 3 + TZ 1; the b116 plant set 1-2 and the b616 plant set 2 (OLD and NEW in one call each) plus the K-series 1 and the controls 1; the hog proof 2; hog cells: b116 file 2 (head x12, main x6, one container each), engine file 6, chain 4; `unit.sh ci` 2; prettier/eslint/typecheck 3; the optional db group 2. About 40 starts; the hog chain runs take about 12 minutes each.** Remove ONLY your own `pc-b993-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name.

## NOT TESTED BY DESIGN (state each unless you do better)
The product's behaviour with a real slow digest (the row stubs `crypto.subtle.digest`), a real browser, a hosted or Linux-runner run, `ci:node` x10 (this gate runs 2 per side), the host busy loops of the ticket's wording (load 13-14; the gate's hog is the container-capped one), the `packages/db` group beyond the one file (C3c is optional), the 164-row contract file, every scanner shape beyond the twelve and the K-series, the demo VM or any hosted host, a locale run, hosted CodeQL beyond the read of the PR's runs (no `codeql` CLI here), other seats' lanes.

## HOLDS
Datasec / Security Composer only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production host or the demo site, not even a GET** (your containers are local, no published port). Network: your one in-clone `git fetch`, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, the in-process Jira GET of C7, cached `docker build` layers, nothing else; `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run`, `gh pr comment`, `gh pr merge`, `gh pr edit` and any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are forbidden; never dismiss an alert. Git in `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`: ls-remote, log, show, diff, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-parse, rev-list, merge-base, grep, config --get); clone, fetch, worktree add and merge-tree only inside `.tools/b993/repo` and `.tools/wt-b993-*`. **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` contents or `inbound/` folders (the unit step's SOW input only as a read-only bind mount, `[ -f ]` only). No Jira write. No decision-queue tool, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test and the in-process read of the Jira client; never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (`rm`, `branch -D`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `prune`): quarantine to `.tools/b993/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they hold a space and `!`); no unquoted word starting with `=`; multi-step chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; read your scripts back and scan for non-ASCII. Scratch changes live ONLY in `wt-b993-mut`, a container's own layer and `.tools/b993/scratch/`; never in the PR tree. Synthetic data only. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"; do not quote git author fields), no card slug, clock from `date`. Nothing to any human. **STANDING LINES:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (your STATUS carries a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read of the builder lane (B985 STATUS and kit), the earlier gates of these two files (B659 and B755 STATUS first lines and verdicts; B899 for the method) and what you reuse; a READY-class verdict without one is returned); no message to any human; Jira writes none; never delete (quarantine). **RESUME at about 80% of context or at the hard stop:** write `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` sections (each check done/partial/not started with evidence paths; next commands; every scratch tree and plant with its restore proof; both locks released, or named if held; any hog container stopped), stop your processes and containers, end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the one question "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". **Usage pause:** a session ended by the weekly limit is the platform, not a STOP; on resume re-read your STATUS last line, re-pin main, the head and the checks.

