## LANDING (Tuesday's, not the gate's; the gate quotes it in FOR TUESDAY and never runs it)
Composer lands by SQUASH, head-pinned, after the gate says GO or GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS and a real green scan of the head through the org ruleset (never bypassed, no alert dismissed). Source: `1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md` line 1799: "squash-merges PR #88 pinned to head 2da99cab after re-reading CodeQL and the checks. Nothing is deployed (Composer deploys only on your card)." Tuesday writes the squash subject AND body explicitly and lands with `gh pr merge 106 -R datasecau/Datasec-Security-Composer --squash --match-head-commit 642a04729baa7a709531ba6617de12d2aa6d21f2 --subject '<subject> (#106)' --body-file <f>`; the body = the two commit messages condensed with any clause graded false replaced, then ONE attribution line and no other trailer; no person's name, ticket key, work number or PR number in the body. Verify after the merge: exactly one co-author line (the noreply address), `localdomain` 0 (control: the same read on `cbe86ba61a45ed776122bf4ee31fd682a0244c1a` prints 1), the parent is the main merged against, and its tree is the head's tree `8a912fe8c59405df59910d050cb6310bfd1e50b1`. If `localdomain` is not 0 do not amend or rewrite main: report it and stop. A merge to main is not a deploy; the records seat moves the tickets.

